<title>USA: TABLE-Lone Star Industries Q2 EPS rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Lone Star Industries Q2 EPS rises.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 Months</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			   $1.53		    $1.26</p>
<p> Net			 $20,181		  $17,263</p>
<p> Revs		     $104,618		 $102,307</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   10,994		   11,427</p>
<p>3  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $1.55		    $1.05</p>
<p> Net			$20,445		  $13,987</p>
<p> Revs		    $165,454		 $155,294</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  10,924		   11,451</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: -- In Q2 1997, construction aggregates operations reported sales for first half 1997 of $19.2 million, a $2.6 million increase from the first half of 1996.  For the same six-month period of 1997 these operations recorded a loss at the gross profit level of $0.2 million as compared to a gross profit of $0.1 million in 1996. The lower results from the construction aggregates operations reflect lower average sales prices due to customer and product mix and higher distribution costs.</p>
</text>
